{
  "name": "Summarize RB2B website visitors in Slack with Claude",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -490,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 800,
        "content": "## Website Visitor Daily Digest (n8n + Claude)\n\n**Who it's for:** You use RB2B to see who visits your site, but the one-at-a-time alerts are\neasy to tune out.\n\n**What it does:** Each visitor is logged to Google Sheets as they arrive. Every morning, Claude\nturns the previous day's visits into one short Slack update with the busiest pages and the\npeople worth following up with.\n\n### How it works\n1. RB2B sends each identified visitor to the webhook.\n2. Google Sheets logs the visitor, landing page, and time right away.\n3. A schedule trigger reads the sheet every morning.\n4. A Filter keeps only yesterday's rows.\n5. An Aggregate node groups those rows into one payload.\n6. Claude summarizes the day and picks the people worth contacting.\n7. Slack posts the finished digest to your channel.\n\n### Setup\n- Connect Google Sheets, Slack and Anthropic.\n- Copy the webhook Production URL into RB2B under Integrations, n8n.\n- Replace the Sheet ID and set your Slack channel in Config.\n- Send a test event from RB2B, check that the row lands, then turn it on."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        30,
        500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 470,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### Setup\nPaste the webhook Production URL into RB2B, then set your Slack channel in **Config (edit me)**. Replace the Sheet ID and connect Sheets, Slack and Anthropic."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        30,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 510,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### 1. Log each visitor as they arrive\nRB2B sends each identified visitor to the webhook. Google Sheets records the visit right away, whether or not the morning digest has run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        770,
        500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 710,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### 2. Gather yesterday's visits\nEvery morning, the workflow reads the sheet, keeps yesterday's rows and groups them into one payload for Claude."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1490,
        500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 510,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### 3. Write and post the digest\nClaude summarizes the visits, counts the busiest pages and picks the people worth contacting. Slack gets the finished update."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1450,
        740
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 430,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### Model Selection\nCurrently using Claude but feel free to substitute a model of your choosing"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "name": "RB2B Visitor Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        60,
        180
      ],
      "webhookId": "rb2b-visitor-feed",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "rb2b-visitor",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "name": "Log Visit to Sheets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        340,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "page": "={{ $json.body['Captured URL'] }}",
            "email": "={{ $json.body['Business Email'] }}",
            "title": "={{ $json.body['Title'] }}",
            "company": "={{ $json.body['Company Name'] }}",
            "seen_at": "={{ $json.body['Seen At'] || $now.toISO() }}",
            "industry": "={{ $json.body['Industry'] }}",
            "referrer": "={{ $json.body['Referrer'] }}",
            "last_name": "={{ $json.body['Last Name'] }}",
            "first_name": "={{ $json.body['First Name'] }}",
            "linkedin_url": "={{ $json.body['LinkedIn URL'] }}",
            "employee_count": "={{ $json.body['Employee Count'] }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow"
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Visitors",
          "cachedResultName": "Visitors"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "name": "Every Morning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        60,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "n4",
      "name": "Config (edit me)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        300,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "slack_channel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#website-visitors"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "focus",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "We sell websites and automation to small service businesses. Pricing and case study pages matter most. Ignore anyone from a competing agency."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "n5",
      "name": "Read Visitors from Sheets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        800,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "operation": "read",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "Visitors",
          "cachedResultName": "Visitors"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "n6",
      "name": "Keep Yesterday Only",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        1040,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 1,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "contains"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.seen_at }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $now.minus({ days: 1 }).toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "n7",
      "name": "Roll Up the Day",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.aggregate",
      "position": [
        1280,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "aggregate": "aggregateAllItemData"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n8",
      "name": "Summarize the Visitors",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1520,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Turn yesterday's identified website visits into a short morning update for the sales team.\n\nFOCUS:\n{{ $('Config (edit me)').item.json.focus }}\n\nVISITOR ROWS (JSON):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.data) }}\n\nTASK:\n1. Summarize who visited yesterday in 2-3 sentences.\n2. List the most-visited pages and the visit count for each one.\n3. Pick up to 5 people worth contacting today. Include their company and the specific activity that made them stand out.\n4. Return outreach_text as a plain-text bullet list. If nobody is a good fit, return \"- No one to follow up with from yesterday\".",
        "messages": {},
        "promptType": "define",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
    {
      "id": "n9",
      "name": "Anthropic Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "position": [
        1480,
        860
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
          "cachedResultName": "Claude Sonnet 4.6"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.4
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.5
    },
    {
      "id": "n10",
      "name": "Structured Output Parser",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "position": [
        1680,
        860
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"summary\": \"31 identified visitors yesterday, 9 from agencies and 4 repeat visits. Pricing was the busiest page.\",\n  \"top_pages\": [\n    {\n      \"page\": \"/pricing\",\n      \"visits\": 11\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outreach\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Dana Reyes\",\n      \"company\": \"Northline Dental\",\n      \"why\": \"Read pricing twice and came back to the case studies page.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outreach_text\": \"- Dana Reyes (Northline Dental): read pricing twice and came back to case studies.\"\n}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "n11",
      "name": "Post the Digest to Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        1800,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=*Website visitors from yesterday*\n\n{{ $json.output.summary }}\n\n*People to follow up with*\n{{ $json.output.outreach_text }}",
